{"author":{"id":"2eecc7d99b502c158aacb0868dca9358610edc02724d21fe49b0196402d3364e"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1788161286,"nonce":"pCbtoGjUEUPQybCkAHtKSnXF0JQ=","title":"ci: a UI-only change rebuilds all four container images — only `scarab-server` embeds the UI","message":"`image.yml`'s `pull_request.paths` includes `ui/**`, and the build is a matrix\nover all four images × two arches. So editing a stylesheet rebuilds\n`scarab-clone`, `scarab-results-sidecar` and `scarab-wsfetch` — none of which\ncontain any UI — on both amd64 and arm64.\n\nOnly `scarab-server` embeds the web UI, so only it needs to watch `ui/**`.\n\nMeasured on PR #3 (UI + one shell script): 8 build jobs, ~3.0 runner-minutes\ntotal. Individually cheap because the layer cache is working; the cost is that\n8 of the PR's 15 checks were irrelevant to it, which makes the check list hard\nto read and trains everyone to ignore it.\n\nFix: derive the matrix from what changed rather than filtering the whole\nworkflow — the `changes` job from the path-filter ticket can emit which images\nto build, with `ui/**` mapping to `scarab-server` only, `docker/clone/**` to\n`scarab-clone`, and so on. `crates/**`, `Cargo.*` and `openapi.json` stay\nmapped to every image that links the workspace.\n\nKeep the arch matrix as-is — it is native-runner multi-arch and already fast.","files":null}]}